  "stem": "The equation \\(5^{n + 2} - 5^{n} = k \\cdot 5^{n}\\), where \\(k\\) is a constant, is true for all values of \\(n\\). What is the value of \\(k\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "24"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Write \\(5^{n + 2}\\) as \\(5^{n} \\cdot 5^{2} = 25 \\cdot 5^{n}\\).",
    "Factor out \\(5^{n}\\): \\(25 \\cdot 5^{n} - 5^{n} = 24 \\cdot 5^{n}\\), so \\(k = 24\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "n = symbols('n', real=True)\nk = simplify((5**(n + 2) - 5**n)/5**n)\nassert k == 24\nassert [Rational(v) for v in spr_answers] == [24]",
